If $n \pmod 3 = 0$, Vanya moves to 1 or 2. Neither is 0. Vanya doesn't win.
If $n \pmod 3 = 1$, Vanya can move to $1+1=2$ or $1-1=0$. If he moves to 0, he wins. So if $n \equiv 1 \pmod 3$, Vanya wins immediately.
If $n \pmod 3 = 2$, Vanya can move to $2+1=0$ or $2-1=1$. If he moves to 0, he wins. So if $n \equiv 2 \pmod 3$, Vanya wins immediately.

So, if $n \pmod 3 \neq 0$, Vanya wins on the first move.
